amitls.library/background                         amitls.library/background

   PURPOSE

   amitls.library is an AmigaOS TLS client shared library wrapping BearSSL.
   Applications hold opaque TlsContext and TlsConnection handles; BearSSL
   engine structures, x509 contexts, and socket I/O buffers are never exposed.

   amitls does not perform DNS lookup, TCP connect(), or close() on sockets.
   The caller opens bsdsocket.library, connects a TCP socket, passes the fd
   to TlsAttachSocketA(), and closes the socket after TlsShutdown() and
   DisposeTlsConnection().

   BOOTSTRAP

   OpenLibrary(AMITLSNAME, AMITLSVERSION) opens dos.library and
   utility.library internally.  bsdsocket.library is caller-owned: open it
   in your task and pass the base to TlsTaskAttach(), following the AmiSSL
   AmiSSL_SocketBase model.

   API TIERS

   Tier 0 — TlsBaseTagsA / TlsBaseTags / TlsError
     Per-process defaults (CA bundle path, verify policy, break mask).

   Tier 1 — TlsTaskAttach, TlsContext
     Per-Exec-task socket/errno binding and persistent TLS settings (verify
     policy, CA bundle override, optional cert hook).

   Tier 2 — TlsConnection  (primary API)
     Attach TLS to an existing TCP socket, complete handshake, stream
     encrypted read/write.  Used by amihttp.library for HTTPS and by any
     protocol client over TLS.

   Tier 3 — Trust store
     PEM CA bundle loading via tags or TlsLoadCABundle().  In-memory cert
     add (TlsAddTrustedCert) is reserved.

   TYPICAL TIER 2 FLOW

   TlsBase = OpenLibrary(AMITLSNAME, AMITLSVERSION);
   SocketBase = OpenLibrary("bsdsocket.library", 4);
   TlsTaskAttach(SocketBase, (APTR)&errno);
   {
       struct TagItem basetags[] = {
           { ATBT_CA_BUNDLE_PATH, (ULONG)"RAM:mozilla.pem" },
           { TAG_DONE, 0 }
       };
       TlsBaseTagsA(basetags);
   }

   ctx = NewTlsContextA(NULL);             /* or NewTlsContext(TAG_DONE) */
   conn = NewTlsConnection(ctx);
   sock = /* socket() + connect() to host:443 in caller code */;
   TlsAttachSocket(conn, sock, hostname,
       ATTA_SSL_VERIFY, ATSSL_VERIFY_PEER, TAG_DONE);
   TlsWrite(conn, request, request_len);   /* handshake completes here */
   while ((n = TlsRead(conn, buf, sizeof(buf), 30)) > 0) {
       /* process buf[0..n-1] */
   }
   TlsShutdown(conn);
   close(sock);
   DisposeTlsConnection(conn);
   DisposeTlsContext(ctx);
   TlsTaskDetach();
   CloseLibrary(TlsBase);

   DEFERRED HANDSHAKE (TlsHandshake before first TlsWrite)

   TlsAttachSocketA(conn, sock, hostname, NULL);
   TlsHandshake(conn, 30);                 /* revision 2+ / ABI v1.1 */
   TlsRead(conn, greeting, sizeof(greeting), 5);  /* TLS app data */
   TlsWrite(conn, request, request_len);

   NON-BLOCKING / LAYERED I/O (amihttp async)

   TlsAttachSocket(conn, sock, hostname,
       ATTA_NON_BLOCKING, TRUE,
       ATTA_EXTERNAL_WAIT, TRUE,
       TAG_DONE);
   rc = TlsHandshake(conn, 30);            /* or TlsWrite for inline handshake */
   while (rc == ERROR_TLS_WANT_READ || rc == ERROR_TLS_WANT_WRITE) {
       WaitSelect on sock;
       rc = TlsHandshake(conn, 30);       /* retry same call */
   }
   /* ATTA_EXTERNAL_WAIT affects TlsHandshake and TlsRead only; TlsWrite uses
      ATTA_NON_BLOCKING for WANT_READ/WRITE during handshake and app data. */

   OWNERSHIP AND LIFETIME

   - TlsTaskAttach() once per Exec task that performs TLS I/O; pair with
     TlsTaskDetach() when the task is done (refcounted — nested attach OK).
   - DisposeTlsContext() only after all TlsConnection handles referencing
     it are disposed.
   - NewTlsConnection(NULL) creates an internal TlsContext owned by the
     connection; DisposeTlsConnection() frees it automatically.
   - The library never closes the TCP socket fd; caller owns sock for its
     entire lifetime.
   - struct TlsPeerCert strings from TlsGetPeerCert() are caller-owned;
     free with TlsPeerCertFree().

   ERROR MODEL

   Two scopes:
     TlsError() — bootstrap, task attach, context allocation, trust path
         configuration, and TlsAttachSocketA failures.
     TlsGetLastError(conn) — authoritative for TlsRead/TlsWrite/TlsHandshake/
         TlsShutdown on that connection.

   Success: TlsRead/TlsWrite return a positive byte count (always below
   ERROR_TLS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED, 8800).  Failure: return an ERROR_TLS_* code
   (8800..8816) as the function result — not a separate negative errno.
   Non-blocking mode may return ERROR_TLS_WANT_READ or ERROR_TLS_WANT_WRITE;
   WaitSelect on the raw TCP fd and retry the same call.

   TlsRead does not return 0 on EOF in the current implementation; an idle or
   closed connection eventually returns ERROR_TLS_READ_TIMEOUT or
   ERROR_TLS_READ_FAILED.

   See amitls.library/errors.

   INCLUDE FILES

   #include <libraries/amitls.h>
   #include <proto/amitls.h>

   SEE ALSO
       amitls.library/tags, amitls.library/errors, amitls.library/hooks,
       SDK/Examples/ATlsTest.c, amihttp.library/background

amitls.library/errors                             amitls.library/errors

   GENERAL INFORMATION

   amitls.library defines ERROR_TLS_* codes in the 8800 range.  After any
   LVO whose return value is an ERROR_TLS_* code (8800..8816), call TlsError()
   or TlsGetLastError(conn) as appropriate.  TlsGetErrorString(code) returns a
   static English description.

   CODES

   ERROR_TLS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED (8800)
       Feature or LVO not yet implemented (e.g. TlsAddTrustedCert).

   ERROR_TLS_DNS_FAILED (8801)
       Reserved — amitls does not perform DNS; caller resolves hostnames.

   ERROR_TLS_CONNECT_FAILED (8802)
       Reserved — TCP connect is caller-owned.

   ERROR_TLS_CONNECT_TIMEOUT (8803)
       TlsHandshake engine retry limit exceeded (ATLS_TLS_IO_TRIES).

   ERROR_TLS_HANDSHAKE (8804)
       TLS handshake failed, TlsAttachSocketA engine init failed, or
       TlsRead/TlsWrite called before handshake completed.

   ERROR_TLS_VERIFY (8805)
       Certificate chain verification failed (no anchors, untrusted chain,
       or bad signature).  Hostname/SNI matching is not yet enforced beyond
       BearSSL chain validation.  Call TlsGetCertVerifyDetail(conn) for the
       BearSSL brerr code.

   ERROR_TLS_READ_TIMEOUT (8806)
       TlsRead exhausted internal retries (timeout_secs 0) or WaitSelect
       timed out (timeout_secs > 0).

   ERROR_TLS_WRITE_FAILED (8807)
       Encrypted send failed after handshake completed.

   ERROR_TLS_READ_FAILED (8808)
       Encrypted read failed (non-WANT error from BearSSL/socket layer).

   ERROR_TLS_ABORTED (8809)
       Reserved for future abort/cancel support.

   ERROR_TLS_PROTOCOL (8810)
       TLS protocol error (e.g. TlsGetPeerCert when no certificate present).

   ERROR_TLS_OUT_OF_MEMORY (8811)
       Memory allocation failed.

   ERROR_TLS_INVALID_URL (8812)
       Reserved — URL parsing is not an amitls concern.

   ERROR_TLS_INVALID_HANDLE (8813)
       Bad or disposed handle, or NULL required argument.

   ERROR_TLS_IO (8814)
       bsdsocket I/O error (including missing/unreadable CA bundle file),
       or TlsAttachSocketA/TlsRead/TlsWrite/TlsHandshake/TlsShutdown without
       a prior TlsTaskAttach on the current Exec task.

   ERROR_TLS_WANT_READ (8815)
       Non-blocking: engine needs socket read before retrying same call.

   ERROR_TLS_WANT_WRITE (8816)
       Non-blocking: engine needs socket write before retrying same call.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsError(), TlsGetLastError(), TlsGetErrorString(),
       TlsGetCertVerifyDetail()

amitls.library/hooks                               amitls.library/hooks

   GENERAL INFORMATION

   Certificate verification hooks are configured with SetTlsContextAttrsA()
   ATSA_CERT_HOOK.  The hook pointer is stored on TlsContext but is not yet
   invoked by the library (reserved for v2, mirroring amihttp HTHK_CERT_VERIFY).

   HOOK TYPES

   ATHK_CERT_VERIFY (1)       — reserved; not yet dispatched.

   PLANNED MESSAGE (v2)

   When implemented, the library will dispatch via utility.library
   CallHookPkt() with a message struct carrying the TlsConnection, filled
   TlsPeerCert, BearSSL verify result, and an BOOL accept override.

   SEE ALSO
       SetTlsContextAttrsA(), ATSA_CERT_HOOK, TlsGetPeerCert(),
       amihttp.library/hooks

amitls.library/tags                                 amitls.library/tags

   GENERAL INFORMATION

   TagItem-based configuration uses TlsBaseTagsA(), NewTlsContextA(),
   SetTlsContextAttrsA(), and TlsAttachSocketA().  Variadic wrappers
   TlsBaseTags(), NewTlsContext(), SetTlsContextAttrs(), and
   TlsAttachSocket() are compiler tagcall/macros over the same LVOs.
   All tag lists are terminated with TAG_DONE.

   ATBT_* — TlsBaseTagsA (Tier 0)

   ATBT_ERRNOPTR
       Default errno pointer for TlsTaskAttach() when errno_ptr is NULL.
       Also copied into per-task state at attach time.  Does not mirror
       TlsError() automatically.

   ATBT_SSL_VERIFY
       Process-wide default verify policy: ATSSL_VERIFY_NONE,
       ATSSL_VERIFY_PEER (default at OpenLibrary), or
       ATSSL_VERIFY_PEER_STRICT (currently treated like PEER).
       Overridden per context (ATSA) or per attach (ATTA).

   ATBT_CA_BUNDLE_PATH
       STRPTR path to a PEM file containing trusted CA certificates.
       Required before ATSSL_VERIFY_PEER handshakes succeed.  No implicit
       default path — caller must set this or ATSA_CA_BUNDLE_PATH.  File is
       parsed lazily into a shared trust cache on first VERIFY_PEER attach.

   ATBT_BREAKMASK
       Exec signal mask stored on the library base (e.g. SIGBREAKF_CTRL_C).
       Not yet polled during blocking I/O — reserved for v2.

   ATBT_LOG_HOOK
       Reserved for v2 diagnostic hook.

   ATSA_* — NewTlsContextA / SetTlsContextAttrsA (Tier 1)

   ATSA_SSL_VERIFY
       Per-context verify policy override.

   ATSA_CIPHER_POLICY
       ATCP_DEFAULT, ATCP_MODERN, or ATCP_COMPAT — stored on TlsContext,
       reserved for v2 (no effect on cipher list today).

   ATSA_ALPN
       STRPTR ALPN protocol list — stored but not yet sent on the wire.

   ATSA_CERT_HOOK
       struct Hook * for ATHK_CERT_VERIFY — stored, not yet invoked.

   ATSA_CA_BUNDLE_PATH
       Per-context PEM CA bundle override.  Clears cached per-context anchors
       when changed.  Falls back to ATBT_CA_BUNDLE_PATH via atls_context_ca_path()
       when unset.  Parsed lazily on first VERIFY_PEER attach.

   ATTA_* — TlsAttachSocketA (Tier 2)

   ATTA_SSL_VERIFY
       Per-connection verify policy override for this attach.

   ATTA_NON_BLOCKING
       When TRUE, socket recv/send use non-blocking semantics and
       TlsRead/TlsWrite may return ERROR_TLS_WANT_READ/WRITE instead of
       blocking internally.

   ATTA_EXTERNAL_WAIT
       When TRUE (ABI v1.1, library revision 2+), TlsHandshake and TlsRead
       do not call WaitSelect internally when the engine needs more wire I/O;
       they return ERROR_TLS_WANT_READ/WRITE and the caller must wait on the
       raw TCP fd and retry.  Does not affect TlsWrite — pair TlsWrite with
       ATTA_NON_BLOCKING for non-blocking handshake/app sends.  Required for
       layered timeout/abort polling (amihttp ht_wait_socket_io).

   ATSSL_VERIFY_* values

   ATSSL_VERIFY_NONE           0 — insecure x509 engine (no chain validation).
   ATSSL_VERIFY_PEER           1 — BearSSL x509_minimal chain validation against
                                   loaded CA anchors; fails when bundle missing
                                   or empty (ERROR_TLS_VERIFY at attach).
   ATSSL_VERIFY_PEER_STRICT    2 — stored and resolved like PEER today; strict
                                   hostname policy reserved for v2.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsBaseTagsA(), NewTlsContextA(), SetTlsContextAttrsA(),
       TlsAttachSocketA(), amitls.library/background

amitls.library/TlsBaseTagsA                   amitls.library/TlsBaseTagsA

   NAME
       TlsBaseTagsA -- Set per-process library defaults.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       rc = TlsBaseTagsA(tags);
       D0                    A0

       LONG TlsBaseTagsA(struct TagItem *tags);

       rc = TlsBaseTags(Tag1, ...);

       LONG TlsBaseTags(Tag firstTag, ...);

   FUNCTION
       Configures process-wide defaults after OpenLibrary().  Tags are
       ATBT_* values; see amitls.library/tags.  TlsBaseTags() is the
       varargs wrapper for the same LVO.

   INPUTS
       tags - TagItem array terminated with TAG_DONE, or NULL.
              Variadic form: tag/data pairs ending in TAG_DONE.

   RESULT
       rc - 0 on success, ERROR_TLS_INVALID_HANDLE on bad library base.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsError(), amitls.library/tags, TlsLoadCABundle(), TlsBaseTags()

amitls.library/TlsError                               amitls.library/TlsError

   NAME
       TlsError -- Return current library error code.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       code = TlsError();
       D0

       LONG TlsError(VOID);

   FUNCTION
       Returns the most recent ERROR_TLS_* code stored on the library base.
       Updated by TlsTaskAttach failures, context allocation, trust path LVOs,
       and TlsAttachSocketA (also mirrored to TlsGetLastError on the conn).
       Cleared to 0 on successful TlsBaseTagsA, TlsTaskAttach,
       SetTlsContextAttrsA, and successful TlsAttachSocketA.  TlsRead/TlsWrite/
       TlsHandshake failures update TlsGetLastError(conn) only — not TlsError().

   RESULT
       code - 0 if no error, otherwise ERROR_TLS_* value.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsGetLastError(), TlsGetErrorString(), amitls.library/errors

amitls.library/TlsGetErrorString             amitls.library/TlsGetErrorString

   NAME
       TlsGetErrorString -- English text for an error code.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       str = TlsGetErrorString(code);
       D0                      D0

       STRPTR TlsGetErrorString(LONG code);

   FUNCTION
       Returns a static string describing an ERROR_TLS_* code.

   INPUTS
       code - ERROR_TLS_* value, or 0 for "No error".

   RESULT
       str - read-only description string.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsError(), TlsGetLastError(), amitls.library/errors

amitls.library/TlsTaskAttach                     amitls.library/TlsTaskAttach

   NAME
       TlsTaskAttach -- Bind bsdsocket to current Exec task.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       rc = TlsTaskAttach(SocketBase, errno_ptr);
       D0                       A0           A1

       LONG TlsTaskAttach(struct Library *SocketBase, APTR errno_ptr);

   FUNCTION
       Registers the current Exec task for TLS I/O.  Snapshots SocketBase and
       errno_ptr into per-task state; each subsequent I/O call runs
       SocketBaseTagList(SBTC_ERRNOPTR/SBTC_HERRNOLONGPTR) on that base via
       atls_sock_configure_errno().

       Must be called once per task before TlsAttachSocketA, TlsRead,
       TlsWrite, TlsHandshake, or TlsShutdown.  Refcounted — repeated
       attach on the same task increments the count.

       If SocketBase is NULL, uses the last non-NULL base stored on the
       library from a prior attach.  If errno_ptr is NULL, uses ATBT_ERRNOPTR
       or the linker-visible global errno symbol.

   INPUTS
       SocketBase - bsdsocket.library base from OpenLibrary(), or NULL.
       errno_ptr  - pointer to int errno for this task, or NULL.

   RESULT
       rc - 0 on success, ERROR_TLS_IO if no socket base available,
           ERROR_TLS_OUT_OF_MEMORY, or ERROR_TLS_INVALID_HANDLE.

   NOTES
       TlsAttachSocketA without a prior TlsTaskAttach on the same task
       returns ERROR_TLS_IO.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsTaskDetach(), TlsAttachSocketA(), amitls.library/background

amitls.library/TlsTaskDetach                     amitls.library/TlsTaskDetach

   NAME
       TlsTaskDetach -- Release per-task TLS runtime.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       TlsTaskDetach();
       void

       VOID TlsTaskDetach(VOID);

   FUNCTION
       Decrements the current task's attach refcount and removes per-task
       state when the count reaches zero.  Does not close bsdsocket.library
       (caller-owned).

   SEE ALSO
       TlsTaskAttach()

amitls.library/NewTlsContextA                     amitls.library/NewTlsContextA

   NAME
       NewTlsContextA -- Allocate a TLS settings context.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       ctx = NewTlsContextA(tags);
       D0                    A0

       struct TlsContext *NewTlsContextA(struct TagItem *tags);

       ctx = NewTlsContext(Tag1, ...);

       struct TlsContext *NewTlsContext(Tag firstTag, ...);

   FUNCTION
       Creates a Tier 1 context inheriting ATBT_* defaults (verify policy
       ATSSL_VERIFY_PEER, no CA bundle until configured).  Optional tags
       are ATSA_* values applied at creation; see amitls.library/tags.
       NewTlsContext() is the varargs wrapper for the same LVO.

   INPUTS
       tags - TagItem list, or NULL for defaults only.
              Variadic form: tag/data pairs ending in TAG_DONE
              (NewTlsContext(TAG_DONE) for defaults).

   RESULT
       ctx - opaque handle, or NULL on failure (TlsError()).

   SEE ALSO
       DisposeTlsContext(), SetTlsContextAttrsA(), NewTlsConnection(),
       NewTlsContext()

amitls.library/DisposeTlsContext             amitls.library/DisposeTlsContext

   NAME
       DisposeTlsContext -- Free a TLS context.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       DisposeTlsContext(ctx);
                         A0

       VOID DisposeTlsContext(struct TlsContext *ctx);

   FUNCTION
       Frees context state including cached trust anchors and ALPN string.
       All TlsConnection handles referencing this context must be disposed
       first (except connections that own an internal context via
       NewTlsConnection(NULL)).

   INPUTS
       ctx - from NewTlsContextA(), or NULL (no action).

   SEE ALSO
       NewTlsContextA()

amitls.library/SetTlsContextAttrsA         amitls.library/SetTlsContextAttrsA

   NAME
       SetTlsContextAttrsA -- Configure TLS context.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       rc = SetTlsContextAttrsA(ctx, tags);
       D0                         A0   A1

       LONG SetTlsContextAttrsA(struct TlsContext *ctx, struct TagItem *tags);

       rc = SetTlsContextAttrs(ctx, Tag1, ...);

       LONG SetTlsContextAttrs(struct TlsContext *ctx, ...);

   FUNCTION
       Applies ATSA_* tags.  See amitls.library/tags.
       SetTlsContextAttrs() is the varargs wrapper for the same LVO.

   INPUTS
       ctx  - valid TlsContext handle.
       tags - TagItem list, TAG_DONE terminated.
              Variadic form: tag/data pairs ending in TAG_DONE.

   RESULT
       rc - 0 on success, ERROR_TLS_INVALID_HANDLE when ctx is NULL.

   SEE ALSO
       NewTlsContextA(), amitls.library/tags, SetTlsContextAttrs()

amitls.library/NewTlsConnection               amitls.library/NewTlsConnection

   NAME
       NewTlsConnection -- Create a TLS connection handle.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       conn = NewTlsConnection(ctx);
       D0                        A0

       struct TlsConnection *NewTlsConnection(struct TlsContext *ctx);

   FUNCTION
       Allocates a Tier 2 connection handle.  When ctx is NULL, creates and
       owns an internal TlsContext with library defaults.

   INPUTS
       ctx - parent TlsContext, or NULL to auto-create one.

   RESULT
       conn - opaque handle, or NULL on failure (TlsError()).

   SEE ALSO
       DisposeTlsConnection(), TlsAttachSocketA()

amitls.library/DisposeTlsConnection       amitls.library/DisposeTlsConnection

   NAME
       DisposeTlsConnection -- Free connection state.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       DisposeTlsConnection(conn);
                              A0

       VOID DisposeTlsConnection(struct TlsConnection *conn);

   FUNCTION
       Releases BearSSL engine state and peer certificate cache.  Does not
       close the TCP socket — caller must close(sock) separately.  When the
       connection owns an internal context (NewTlsConnection(NULL)), disposes
       that context too.

   INPUTS
       conn - TlsConnection handle, or NULL.

   SEE ALSO
       NewTlsConnection(), TlsShutdown()

amitls.library/TlsAttachSocketA                 amitls.library/TlsAttachSocketA

   NAME
       TlsAttachSocketA -- Install TLS on an existing TCP socket.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       rc = TlsAttachSocketA(conn, sock, hostname, tags);
       D0                     A0   D0   A1        A2

       LONG TlsAttachSocketA(struct TlsConnection *conn, LONG sock,
           STRPTR hostname, struct TagItem *tags);

       rc = TlsAttachSocket(conn, sock, hostname, Tag1, ...);

       LONG TlsAttachSocket(struct TlsConnection *conn, LONG sock,
           STRPTR hostname, ...);

   FUNCTION
       Initializes BearSSL client engine on sock.  hostname is used for SNI
       (max 255 bytes, NUL-terminated) and must be non-NULL.  Applies ATTA_*
       tags (ATTA_SSL_VERIFY resolved via atls_resolve_verify()).
       TlsAttachSocket() is the varargs wrapper for the same LVO.

       Does not perform the TLS handshake — that completes on the first
       successful TlsWrite(), or explicitly via TlsHandshake() (revision 2+).

       Snapshots the current task's SocketBase/errno into the connection.
       Requires TlsTaskAttach() on the calling Exec task.

       VERIFY_PEER without a loadable CA bundle or with zero anchors returns
       ERROR_TLS_VERIFY during engine init (missing file may surface as
       ERROR_TLS_IO from the trust loader).

   INPUTS
       conn     - TlsConnection handle.
       sock     - connected TCP socket fd from caller's connect().
       hostname - server name for SNI (required, max 255 chars; not DNS-resolved).
       tags     - optional ATTA_* TagItem list, or NULL.

   RESULT
       rc - 0 on success, ERROR_TLS_* on failure.  Sets TlsGetLastError(conn).

   SEE ALSO
       TlsWrite(), TlsHandshake(), TlsTaskAttach(), amitls.library/tags,
       TlsAttachSocket()

   NAME
       TlsHandshake -- Complete TLS handshake without application data.  (V1.1)

   SYNOPSIS
       rc = TlsHandshake(conn, timeout_secs);
       D0                  A0   D0

       LONG TlsHandshake(struct TlsConnection *conn, ULONG timeout_secs);

   FUNCTION
       Drives the BearSSL handshake to completion without sending application
       payload.  Use when the protocol must complete TLS before the first
       TlsWrite (see ATlsTest deferred-handshake coverage).

       When ATTA_EXTERNAL_WAIT is TRUE, returns ERROR_TLS_WANT_READ/WRITE
       instead of blocking; caller WaitSelect's on the socket and retries the
       same TlsHandshake() call.

       timeout_secs is accepted for ABI compatibility but not yet used;
       retry exhaustion returns ERROR_TLS_CONNECT_TIMEOUT.

       Library revision 2+ (AMITLSVERSION 1, revision 2).

   INPUTS
       conn          - TlsConnection after TlsAttachSocketA().
       timeout_secs  - reserved (not yet applied); internal retry limit only.

   RESULT
       rc - 0 on success, ERROR_TLS_* on failure.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsAttachSocketA(), TlsWrite(), ATTA_EXTERNAL_WAIT

amitls.library/TlsRead                                 amitls.library/TlsRead

   NAME
       TlsRead -- Read decrypted application data.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       n = TlsRead(conn, buffer, buflen, timeout_secs);
       D0            A0   A1       D0        D1

       LONG TlsRead(struct TlsConnection *conn, APTR buffer, ULONG buflen,
           ULONG timeout_secs);

   FUNCTION
       Copies up to buflen decrypted bytes into caller buffer.  Returns
       immediately when decrypted data is already buffered (TlsPending > 0).

       Requires completed handshake (TlsWrite or TlsHandshake).  Before
       handshake, returns ERROR_TLS_HANDSHAKE.

       When ATTA_NON_BLOCKING is set, socket-level EWOULDBLOCK maps to
       ERROR_TLS_WANT_READ/WRITE on the r < 0 path.  When ATTA_EXTERNAL_WAIT
       is set and the engine needs wire I/O (r == 0), returns WANT without
       calling WaitSelect.

       timeout_secs: 0 allows up to ATLS_TLS_IO_TRIES internal polls then
       ERROR_TLS_READ_TIMEOUT; >0 uses WaitSelect with that second count
       between polls (unless ATTA_EXTERNAL_WAIT).

   INPUTS
       conn          - TlsConnection after handshake.
       buffer        - destination buffer (caller allocated).
       buflen        - size of buffer in bytes.
       timeout_secs  - read wait timeout in seconds.

   RESULT
       n - bytes read (>0), or ERROR_TLS_* on failure.  Does not return 0 on
           EOF in the current implementation.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsWrite(), TlsPending(), TlsGetLastError()

amitls.library/TlsWrite                               amitls.library/TlsWrite

   NAME
       TlsWrite -- Write encrypted application data.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       n = TlsWrite(conn, buffer, len);
       D0             A0   A1       D0

       LONG TlsWrite(struct TlsConnection *conn, APTR buffer, ULONG len);

   FUNCTION
       Encrypts and sends len bytes.  On the first TlsWrite after
       TlsAttachSocketA(), completes the TLS handshake (client hello through
       finished).  Certificate verification runs during handshake when
       verify policy is not ATSSL_VERIFY_NONE.

       Non-blocking (ATTA_NON_BLOCKING): returns ERROR_TLS_WANT_READ/WRITE
       when the socket would block during handshake or app-data send; retry
       the same TlsWrite() after WaitSelect.  ATTA_EXTERNAL_WAIT does not
       change TlsWrite behaviour.

   INPUTS
       conn   - TlsConnection after TlsAttachSocketA().
       buffer - source data.
       len    - byte count (>0).

   RESULT
       n - len on success (>0), or ERROR_TLS_* on failure.

   NOTES
       A verify failure during handshake returns ERROR_TLS_VERIFY; query
       TlsGetCertVerifyDetail() and TlsGetPeerCert() for diagnostics.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsRead(), TlsAttachSocketA(), TlsHandshake()

amitls.library/TlsPending                           amitls.library/TlsPending

   NAME
       TlsPending -- Decrypted bytes ready without blocking read.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       n = TlsPending(conn);
       D0             A0

       ULONG TlsPending(struct TlsConnection *conn);

   FUNCTION
       Returns count of application data bytes already decrypted in the
       BearSSL engine buffer.  Uses the connection's snapshotted SocketBase
       via atls_conn_bind_io(); does not require TlsTaskAttach on the
       calling task if the snapshot is valid.

   INPUTS
       conn - TlsConnection handle.

   RESULT
       n - pending byte count, or 0 when none or bad handle.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsRead()

amitls.library/TlsShutdown                         amitls.library/TlsShutdown

   NAME
       TlsShutdown -- Send TLS close_notify.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       rc = TlsShutdown(conn);
       D0               A0

       LONG TlsShutdown(struct TlsConnection *conn);

   FUNCTION
       Sends TLS close_notify when the BearSSL engine is active, then marks
       the engine inactive.  Does not close the TCP socket.  Always returns 0
       from the engine layer after a successful task bind.

   INPUTS
       conn - TlsConnection handle.

   RESULT
       rc - 0 on success, ERROR_TLS_INVALID_HANDLE, or ERROR_TLS_IO when
           TlsTaskAttach was not called on the current task.

   SEE ALSO
       DisposeTlsConnection(), close()

amitls.library/TlsGetLastError                 amitls.library/TlsGetLastError

   NAME
       TlsGetLastError -- Per-connection error code.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       code = TlsGetLastError(conn);
       D0                     A0

       LONG TlsGetLastError(struct TlsConnection *conn);

   FUNCTION
       Returns conn->tc_LastError — the last ERROR_TLS_* from I/O on this
       connection.  Authoritative after TlsRead, TlsWrite, TlsHandshake,
       TlsShutdown, and TlsAttachSocketA.  Also updated on TlsTaskAttach
       failures propagated through those entry points.  Separate from
       TlsError() library-base errors.

   INPUTS
       conn - TlsConnection handle.

   RESULT
       code - ERROR_TLS_* or 0.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsError(), TlsGetCertVerifyDetail(), amitls.library/errors

amitls.library/TlsGetCertVerifyDetail   amitls.library/TlsGetCertVerifyDetail

   NAME
       TlsGetCertVerifyDetail -- BearSSL verify error after ERROR_TLS_VERIFY.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       brerr = TlsGetCertVerifyDetail(conn);
       D0                           A0

       LONG TlsGetCertVerifyDetail(struct TlsConnection *conn);

   FUNCTION
       After ERROR_TLS_VERIFY from handshake or write, returns the BearSSL
       brerr code (e.g. BR_ERR_X509_NOT_TRUSTED, BR_ERR_X509_EXPIRED).
       Maps to struct TlsPeerCert.tpc_VerifyResult when peer cert is copied.

   INPUTS
       conn - TlsConnection after failed verify.

   RESULT
       brerr - BearSSL error code, or 0 when unavailable.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsGetPeerCert(), ERROR_TLS_VERIFY, amitls.library/errors

amitls.library/TlsGetPeerCert                   amitls.library/TlsGetPeerCert

   NAME
       TlsGetPeerCert -- Copy TLS peer certificate fields.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       rc = TlsGetPeerCert(conn, cert);
       D0                  A0   A1

       LONG TlsGetPeerCert(struct TlsConnection *conn,
           struct TlsPeerCert *cert);

   FUNCTION
       After handshake, fills struct TlsPeerCert with strdup'd strings from
       the connection cache.  tpc_VerifyResult copies tc_CertVerifyResult
       (BearSSL brerr when verify failed).  Caller must TlsPeerCertFree().

       Before handshake or when tc_CertPresent is FALSE, returns
       ERROR_TLS_PROTOCOL without filling cert fields.

   INPUTS
       conn - TlsConnection after attach (handshake optional).
       cert - caller-allocated struct TlsPeerCert (need not be zeroed).

   RESULT
       rc - 0 on success, ERROR_TLS_INVALID_HANDLE, or ERROR_TLS_PROTOCOL
           when no peer certificate is available.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsPeerCertFree(), struct TlsPeerCert, TlsGetCertVerifyDetail()

amitls.library/TlsPeerCertFree                   amitls.library/TlsPeerCertFree

   NAME
       TlsPeerCertFree -- Free certificate strings from GetPeerCert.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       TlsPeerCertFree(cert);
                       A0

       VOID TlsPeerCertFree(struct TlsPeerCert *cert);

   FUNCTION
       Frees STRPTR fields allocated by TlsGetPeerCert().

   INPUTS
       cert - struct TlsPeerCert from TlsGetPeerCert().

   SEE ALSO
       TlsGetPeerCert()

amitls.library/TlsLoadCABundle                   amitls.library/TlsLoadCABundle

   NAME
       TlsLoadCABundle -- Set process-wide PEM CA bundle path.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       rc = TlsLoadCABundle(path);
       D0                   A0

       LONG TlsLoadCABundle(STRPTR path);

   FUNCTION
       Sets the same process-wide PEM bundle path as ATBT_CA_BUNDLE_PATH.
       Convenience for callers that configure trust via function call instead
       of TlsBaseTagsA().  Does not parse the file until a VERIFY_PEER
       handshake requires anchors.

       amitls does not search for a default bundle — caller must supply a
       path (e.g. Mozilla cacert.pem, RAM:mozilla.pem).

   INPUTS
       path - STRPTR filesystem path to PEM CA file.

   RESULT
       rc - 0 on success, ERROR_TLS_INVALID_HANDLE or ERROR_TLS_OUT_OF_MEMORY.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsBaseTagsA(), ATBT_CA_BUNDLE_PATH, ATSA_CA_BUNDLE_PATH,
       TlsClearTrustedCerts()

amitls.library/TlsAddTrustedCert               amitls.library/TlsAddTrustedCert

   NAME
       TlsAddTrustedCert -- Add in-memory trusted certificate.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       rc = TlsAddTrustedCert(data, len, format);
       D0                     A0   D0   D1

       LONG TlsAddTrustedCert(APTR data, ULONG len, ULONG format);

   FUNCTION
       Not yet implemented.  Returns ERROR_TLS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED.  Use
       ATBT_CA_BUNDLE_PATH / ATSA_CA_BUNDLE_PATH with a PEM file instead.

   INPUTS
       data   - certificate bytes (unused).
       len    - length (unused).
       format - ATCF_DER or ATCF_PEM (unused).

   RESULT
       rc - ERROR_TLS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsLoadCABundle(), amitls.library/tags

amitls.library/TlsClearTrustedCerts         amitls.library/TlsClearTrustedCerts

   NAME
       TlsClearTrustedCerts -- Clear parsed CA anchors and bundle path.  (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
       TlsClearTrustedCerts();
       void

       VOID TlsClearTrustedCerts(VOID);

   FUNCTION
       Frees the process-wide shared trust cache (atb_SharedTrust) and clears
       ATBT_CA_BUNDLE_PATH.  Per-context trust stores are not affected —
       dispose the owning TlsContext or change ATSA_CA_BUNDLE_PATH to clear
       those.

   SEE ALSO
       TlsLoadCABundle(), DisposeTlsContext()
